  * _NET_SUPPORTED stays a list of atoms. sg_x11_workarea added
    _NET_WORKAREA with xprop -set, which cannot write a list: the whole
    list became ONE atom named "_NET_WM_STATE, ..., _NET_WORKAREA", so Qt
    and GTK saw a window manager supporting nothing. SG Office's title bar
    could not be dragged (Qt's startSystemMove needs _NET_WM_MOVERESIZE),
    and _NET_WM_STATE and _NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW went unused. Now
    sg_x11_add_supported appends the atom with Xlib (python3 ctypes);
    without python3 the window manager's list is left alone. Test:
    test/workarea-test.sh now checks each entry is an atom of its own
    (the old xprop -set as a mutant fails it).
  * Linux programs draw through Xwayland: the session tells GTK, Qt, SDL,
    Firefox and Electron to use X11 (GDK_BACKEND=x11, QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb,
    SDL_VIDEODRIVER=x11, MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND=0,
    ELECTRON_OZONE_PLATFORM_HINT=x11), in its environment, the user's
    systemd manager and D-Bus activation (lib/sg-common.sh
    sg_linux_app_env, called by sg-session-start). A native Wayland
    toplevel was shown full screen over the taskbar: GNOME Calculator
    opened from SG Store. Now a normal window with its taskbar button (QA
    VM). Test: make test-linuxappenv (stand-in systemctl and
    dbus-update-activation-environment; mutant NOENV).
  * The SYSTEM account's temporary folder, C:\Windows\SystemTemp, as
    Windows has it: made at every boot by sg-prefix-init, SYSTEM's alone
    (0700, no inherited entries). wine-sg 0638 hands it to SYSTEM
    processes from GetTempPath2; elevated installers (Omaha) unpack there.
    Test: programdata-test (mutant NOSYSTEMTEMP).
  * The session starts sg-compositor's sg-deskcomp (sg_start_deskcomp, from
    sg-run-explorer once the desktop is up): window shadows, real alpha and
    the window effects for Windows programs. SG_DESKCOMP=0 leaves it out.
    Test: test-deskcomp-start (and its mutant without the launch).

