sg-session (0.1.0-82) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The SYSTEM account may write in the prefix's shared trees (Program
    Files, Program Files (x86), ProgramData, users\Public), as SYSTEM may
    anywhere on Windows: a file a program installed or wrote there as the
    user, the elevated reinstall could not replace (Mp3tag: "Could not
    write file"; the Store walk). An ACL entry for the account and a
    default one for later files; the existing trees once. sg-common.sh
    sg_system_access, from sg-prefix-init. Test: test/programdata-test.sh
    (mutant: no entries).
  * The session has a polkit agent: a Linux program that asks to act as an
    administrator (pkexec -- GParted, Timeshift) gets the "Run as
    administrator" consent on the secure surface. Without an agent polkit
    refused at once (the Store walk: GParted, Timeshift). sg-polkit-agent
    runs as the user (sg-session-start) and asks sg-brokerd; after a Yes
    from someone polkit asked for, the broker's root monitor gives polkitd
    the answer (sg-polkit-respond, never for an agent of root's or
    SYSTEM's). The monitor waits for its helpers again (SIGCHLD).
    Test: make test-polkit (private bus, stand-in polkitd; mutants: the
    broker's and the monitor's checks). VM: pkexec id as alex -> consent ->
    uid=0; No -> "Request dismissed".
  * An administrator's session says so to its programs (SG_USER_ADMIN=1 for
    the administrators' group, from sg-session-start): wine-sg 0623 then
    asks for consent for a highestAvailable program, as Windows asks an
    administrator (Geany's installer had installed into the profile). Only
    whether to ask: the broker still checks who answers.
  * sg-wineserver.service: CAP_SYS_PTRACE permitted too, for wine-sg 0624
    (the server traces the SYSTEM account's own processes, which have
    SYSTEM's group, not the prefix's: debuggers and ReadProcessMemory on
    elevated programs; MediaMonkey's setup no longer crashes and hangs).
  * Program Files is the administrators': users may read and run what is
    there, not change it, as on Windows. The prefix gave the Wine group
    (every user) write in Program Files, Program Files (x86) and Common
    Files, so a standard user could replace a program or a DLL that SYSTEM
    or an administrator runs later. sg_program_files_protected (sg-common)
    takes the owning group's write (setfacl g::, so SYSTEM's own entry
    stays); folders an installer shared with the users (setgid: Steam's)
    stay shared. The whole trees once (stamp, cleared when Wine updates
    the prefix), the roots at every boot. Test: test/programdata-test.sh
    (mutants: none; chmod, which took SYSTEM's write too). VM: alex is
    refused, SYSTEM writes, an elevated install (Geany) still works.
  * sg-elevate --ready FILE: the broker's answer ("0" launched, "1"
    declined, "2" failed) goes into FILE as soon as it comes, for wine-sg
    0625's ShellExecuteEx, which now returns once the elevated program has
    started (Total Commander's installer gave up on its elevated copy
    during the consent prompt). /usr/share/stained-glass/sg-elevate.features
    says it can. Test: test/elevate-debug-test.sh (launched, declined).

